{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7HL2uq55LiDyR9tJCZ1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\n**Let's Turn the Lights Back On at the [Cinema Name]**\n\nWhen the [Cinema Name] closed in 2022, it was still selling about 180 tickets a week. People hadn't stopped coming. Since then, seeing a film on the big screen has meant driving to the nearest cinema, 38 miles away.\n\nWe want to bring it back, and this time the numbers add up.\n\n**What we need**\nWe need $85,000 to replace the projector and sound system and repair the roof. If we raise it, the building's owner will rent the cinema to us for $1 a year for 10 years.\n\n**Why it's within reach**\nA local bank has pledged $25,000 if we raise the rest by June 30. That means we need $60,000 from our community, which is half of what we asked for last time.\n\n**About last time**\nThree years ago we tried to raise $120,000. We reached $47,000, fell short, and refunded every dollar. We learned from that. We've cut the goal by $35,000, secured a 10-year lease for almost nothing, and found a partner ready to put in $25,000 once we've done our part. Last time, this town gave $47,000. This time, we need $13,000 more than that.\n\n**Who will run it**\n46 volunteers have already signed up to run the box office and the snack bar. We have the people and the lease. What we still need is a working projector, a sound system and a solid roof.\n\n**How you can help**\nGive what you can before June 30. Share this page. Tell everyone who has made that 38-mile drive just to see a movie.\n\nEach dollar you give gets us closer to $60,000, and reaching $60,000 unlocks the bank's $25,000.\n\nLet's fill those seats again.\n</final_document>\n\nThe pitch is about 300 words. Some things to check before you publish:\n\n- **The $60,000 target:** I worked this out as $85,000 minus the bank's $25,000. Please confirm the bank's pledge works that way and not some other way.\n- **What happens if you fall short:** You refunded everyone last time, so donors will want to know what happens if you miss the goal this time. If you have a policy, like refunds or an all-or-nothing platform, add one line about it. It may help more than anything else in the pitch.\n- **The deadline:** I wrote \"June 30\" with no year. Add \"2027\" if that's when it is, so no one has to guess.\n- **The name:** Replace [Cinema Name] with the cinema's name. If you have a photo of the marquee or the auditorium, put it at the top."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5365,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5365},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2a27bfc-56fe-4ee5-b173-045d6e6185b3","uuid":"b3a105fa-f2c3-4a7b-90c0-30a68e51aec0","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:02:23.384Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7HL2jf439cVy7UxNPdd"}
